A||||9||Fieromarksthespot||Can you swap a 2.8 for a 3.1 from a late model GM product?||||5||
Z||000000||Fieromarksthespot||01-21-2001||12:31 PM||||<BR>I have a blown 2.8 and want to swap for a 3.1 or larger engine. I would like to drop a complete 3.1 from a late model GM product without changing heads etc from my 2.8 can this be done without a huge hassell? I would like to keep the 4 sp auto trans from the new engine.<P>What will I need to do this?  <P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||01-21-2001||12:35 PM||||Do a search and you should find all the info you need and then some. Search is right up by the button to post reply.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fieromarksthespot||01-21-2001||12:54 PM||||<BR>I'll do a search, but I would also like input on my question.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||01-21-2001||02:40 PM||||I have not done this but I think it would be much like the 3800 swap where you have to swap in the computer and do some custom wiring. Unlike the 3800 swap though I think it would bolt up to the fiero engine mounts with little or no modifications. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-21-2001||02:43 PM||||Forgot to click the signature box again and to say you can swap that four speed but I think you have to modify one of the driveshafts to make it fit the fiero chassis.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||01-21-2001||06:19 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Forgot to click the signature box again and to say you can swap that four speed but I think you have to modify one of the driveshafts to make it fit the fiero chassis.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the engine all bolts up same. if you have a stick and you want the new auto, its apparently a big problem, i looked into the trans swap myself, the whole engine wiring harness has to be modified and you have to put in a new instrument panel harness from a auto car. My estimate for the job by Twin Cities Fiero was over $4,000 for just the trans swap. I did do the 3.1 swap but left the original 4 spd, with a new clutch. Apparently the prob is the lock up on trans and if you have cruise control the new auto wont work with the factory harness with a stick.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Lurch||01-21-2001||07:42 PM||||I'm in the middle of this swap.  The engine ecm and harness are out of a 90 Lumina(3.1), and it's going into an 88 coupe with Isuzu 5spd. Have the engine bolted up to trans and am now fiddling with wiring, plumbing etc.  The late style v6 will probably result in a cleaner overall installation.  The water outlets for the radiator are in very similar locations as the 2.5 4cyl.  The 4 cylinder hoses will almost go right on the v6 connections.  It appears that the original 2.8 tube manifolds will fit on the aluminum heads, but the bolt holes need to be slotted where they mount on the heads.  The fiero manifolds also need to be welded/ported because the exhaust ports on the aluminum heads are larger than the iron heads. The fuel rails need to be turned around so the fuel outlets are on the passenger side of the car.  I gutted the 3.1 power steering pump so I could use the serpentine belt setup on the late engine.  The stock alternator position is in the way of the existing dogbone mount, so it will have to be removed.  Haven't decided yet where to mount a torque strut, maybe off alternator mount on the front of engine or off bellhousing bolts.  Either way, I think the forward wall of the trunk would have to be reinforced in some manner to accomodate new torque strut location.  I used a flywheel off a 90 lumina with 5spd (found in junkyard).  Have complete under hood harness and weatherproof ecm and intend to graft late harness and 2.5 harness together and mount ecm in battery area with heatshield between ecm and engine area, with expectation that air will draft up from area under quarter panel by vapor canister upward past ecm and out engine compartment grill.  If this doesn't give enough fresh air by ecm, we'll probably have to rig up a fan arrangement to help.  Other hurdles that have not been cleared yet are:  1. stock fuel lines(steel) don't work very well at front of engine, thinking about rigging up some AN lines from fuel rails to existing steel lines from tank.  2. Signal from Isuzu VSS to new ECM; Don't know if ecm needs accurate VSS signal to work properly. I think later trans used higher pulse/mile VSS than 88 Isuzu trans.<BR>rogergarrison, if you've done this swap, any insight or solutions would be appreciated. <BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fieromarksthespot||01-21-2001||09:08 PM||||<BR>Guys, my car is a 3sp auto and I want to go with a the newer 4sp with the 3.1 engine. Can I use my 2.8's computer? Will I have to do any rewiring? Would a 3.1 from a minivan be a better choice over a 3.1 from a car? <P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||01-21-2001||10:45 PM||||This may seem obvious to you but I'll mention it anyway.  The 4 cyl fuel pump needs to be replaced with one designed for multiport fuel injection unless the 3.1 engine uses a throttle body injector.  V-6 Fiero fuel pumps put out around 45psi while the 4 cyl one puts out around 15 psi.||||reg||1
Z||000009||COUNTIBLIS||01-22-2001||11:29 PM||||Im doing this swap with the 96 beratta engine.  The wiring is a mess.  <BR>||||reg||1
